    "sampleQualification": "A single warmed JIT sample per platform. Each of 2,000 rounds replaces a layer slot with 7 and 9 and verifies both reads. The xlang loop includes checked scopes, snapshot checks, reference operations, and var comparisons. The C loop uses the same native layer and scalar inputs with direct C result checks. Standard C clock() timing is platform-specific and does not isolate individual bridge costs. The first populated slot allocates a 6,656-byte pointer table on x64 and a 16-byte record. One record is allocated per newly populated slot. Container snapshots can copy and allocate according to the value tree.",
